A||N||2||fastonpumpgas||FLyWheel Fun||||1
Z||000000||fastonpumpgas||10-12-1999||07:47 AM||||I am doin gthe 3.1 conversion right now, i was reading some forums and I thought as long as it is a nuetral balanced flywheel it will be ok, is there actaully a differance in the 88 fiero flywheel.  I mean the 90 beretta 3.1 flywheel is the same diameter and teeth, and is a nuetral balanced.  Will it work ok?   ||||reg||1
Z||000001||squid||10-13-1999||11:04 PM||||Look at the side of your stock flywheel opposite the clutch face. If there is the same amount of thickness all the way around then its neutral(there will still be some small balancing holes along the edge).If there is a depression in the wheel shaped like a quarter moon then its externally balanced.If your '88 has aluminum heads its definately internal/neutral.The beretta flywheel will work too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fastonpumpgas||10-14-1999||06:11 PM||||Thanks squid, everybody always says an 88 fiero flywheel, So I did some checking and all 3.1 are nuetral balanced (I think) , bu tthey definately have the same diameter and the same amount of teeth.  I just didnt know if maybe the fiero flywheel was thicker.  I figured they are all the same.  got to love GM  !!!!!   thanks again, they have um at my local bone yard for 50 bucks||||reg||1
